{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;stream_event&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;content_block_stop&quot;,&quot;index&quot;:0},&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;fd165393-2799-476e-a0bf-68daa35ae21c&quot;}
{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;message&quot;:{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;tool_use_id&quot;:&quot;toolu_01B5tfzAZmtJSUfQNthGg7iW&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;tool_result&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;1\t&lt;!--\n2\t  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation\n3\t\n4\t  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.PartialMemberOverrides\n5\t-->\n6\t&lt;block\n7\t  xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n8\t  xmlns:xsi=\&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\&quot;\n9\t  xsi:schemaLocation=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd\n10\t                      \&quot;\n11\t  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n12\t  xmlns:def=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.definition\&quot;\n13\t  xmlns:doc=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.documentation\&quot;>\n14\t\n15\t  &lt;name>PartialMemberOverrides&lt;/name>\n16\t  &lt;type>doc:PartialMemberOverrides&lt;/type>\n17\t  &lt;baseType>core:Documentation&lt;/baseType>\n18\t  &lt;is>A guide to partial member overrides&lt;/is>\n19\t\n20\t  &lt;documentation>\n21\t    Child Blocks override inherited members with override=\&quot;true\&quot;, or satisfy abstract implementation\n22\t    obligations with a locally complete override. The flag is required whenever a local member\n23\t    redeclaration merges with an existing member from the baseType chain or from contracts[] —\n24\t    contract completion uses the same rule as baseType refinement.\n25\t\n26\t    Local declaration properties (never inherited; only effects propagate):\n27\t    • abstract=\&quot;true\&quot; — incomplete declaration; creates an implementation obligation\n28\t    • final=\&quot;true\&quot; — seals the declaration; descendants cannot override\n29\t    • override=\&quot;true\&quot; — confirms deliberate redefinition of an inherited member\n30\t    Boolean properties require an explicit true or false — empty elements and bare attributes are\n31\t    invalid. Preferred literals: lowercase true / false.\n32\t\n33\t    Modes:\n34\t    • new — introduces a member; must not set override=\&quot;true\&quot; → else BML_OVERRIDE_WITHOUT_PARENT\n35\t    • override — refines an inherited member; omit override when merging → BML_OVERRIDE_REQUIRED\n36\t    Each redeclaration layer must set override=\&quot;true\&quot; again — override is not inherited.\n37\t\n38\t    Partial authoring: only the member name, override mode, and changed attributes need to be\n39\t    specified — all other attributes are inherited from the parent definition. Omit unchanged type\n40\t    (and other unchanged attributes such as bml:xml or defaults). On aggregations, restating an\n41\t    identical type when only filling an inherited member → BML_REDUNDANT_AGGREGATION_TYPE (warning\n42\t    V1). Declare type on an override only when refining or replacing the inherited type.\n43\t\n44\t    Abstract → implementation:\n45\t    • Parent may omit required parts (e.g. property without type or value) when abstract=\&quot;true\&quot;\n46\t    • Child implements with override=\&quot;true\&quot; and a locally complete declaration (abstract defaults\n47\t      to false → locally concrete)\n48\t    • To keep a member abstract in a child, redeclare with override=\&quot;true\&quot; abstract=\&quot;true\&quot;\n49\t    • Abstract member left unimplemented on a concrete block → BML_ABSTRACT_MEMBER_NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n50\t    Capability overrides supply a full implementation child element (not a boolean attribute).\n51\t\n52\t    Merge rules (resolveEffectiveMembers — baseType chain → contracts declaration order → local):\n53\t    • Same member kind required (property overrides property, …)\n54\t    • Only specified attrs replaced; unspecified attrs inherited\n55\t    • Override matching key: (resolvedNamespace, normalizedLogicalName) — visibility prefixes\n56\t      stripped; xmlns prefix aliases may differ if they resolve to the same namespace\n57\t    • Visibility may widen (protected → public); narrowing → BML_VISIBILITY_NARROWING\n58\t    • Member-level bml:xml may change on the same override\n59\t    • Private members cannot be overridden → BML_FINAL_MEMBER_OVERRIDE\n60\t    • final=\&quot;true\&quot; on parent prevents override → BML_FINAL_MEMBER_OVERRIDE\n61\t\n62\t    readOnly is orthogonal to final / abstract / override: it controls instance authoring only.\n63\t    • Block definition — may declare and set readOnly members via value, composition, or partial\n64\t      override\n65\t    • Child Block definition — may override an inherited readOnly member (value/composition only;\n66\t      cannot override a final member at all)\n67\t    • Block instance — must not set a member whose effective definition has readOnly=true →\n68\t      BML_READONLY_MEMBER_WRITE (after resolveEffectiveMembers on every BlockInstance)\n69\t    • Expressions — may read readOnly members subject to visibility; renderers may read the BOM\n70\t    A public readOnly member remains publicly readable. final blocks value overrides entirely;\n71\t    readOnly does not.\n72\t\n73\t    Declared on org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition (abstract, final, override, readOnly,\n74\t    visibility) and specialized on PropertyDefinition, AggregationDefinition, AssociationDefinition,\n75\t    and CapabilityDefinition.\n76\t  &lt;/documentation>\n77\t\n78\t  &lt;references>\n79\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:MemberDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;Defines\&quot;>\n80\t      abstract, final, override, readOnly, visibility — local declaration properties.\n81\t    &lt;/see>\n82\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:PropertyDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n83\t      Property override completeness — type and value.\n84\t    &lt;/see>\n85\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:AggregationDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n86\t      Aggregation overrides — omit unchanged type; composition fill.\n87\t    &lt;/see>\n88\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:CapabilityDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n89\t      Capability overrides — implementation child element.\n90\t    &lt;/see>\n91\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:MemberVisibility\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n92\t      Visibility widening and private override prohibition.\n93\t    &lt;/see>\n94\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:ModelingGuidelines\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n95\t      Contracts merge order and abstract/final patterns.\n96\t    &lt;/see>\n97\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:MemberAuthoring\&quot; relation=\&quot;ReadNext\&quot;>\n98\t      Next — definition fields vs instance payloads (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; / &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;).\n99\t    &lt;/see>\n100\t  &lt;/references>\n101\t\n102\t&lt;/block>\n103\t&quot;}]},&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;121f22f7-23cc-4945-bf36-edba1e007caf&quot;,&quot;timestamp&quot;:&quot;2026-09-03T21:58:59.814Z&quot;,&quot;tool_use_result&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;file&quot;:{&quot;filePath&quot;:&quot;/Users/pksoftware/workspace-fh/blockml/node_modules/@blockml/core/blocks/org/blockml/bml/documentation/PartialMemberOverrides.bml&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;&lt;!--\n  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation\n\n  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.PartialMemberOverrides\n-->\n&lt;block\n  xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n  xmlns:xsi=\&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\&quot;\n  xsi:schemaLocation=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd\n                      \&quot;\n  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n  xmlns:def=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.definition\&quot;\n  xmlns:doc=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.documentation\&quot;>\n\n  &lt;name>PartialMemberOverrides&lt;/name>\n  &lt;type>doc:PartialMemberOverrides&lt;/type>\n  &lt;baseType>core:Documentation&lt;/baseType>\n  &lt;is>A guide to partial member overrides&lt;/is>\n\n  &lt;documentation>\n    Child Blocks override inherited members with override=\&quot;true\&quot;, or satisfy abstract implementation\n    obligations with a locally complete override. The flag is required whenever a local member\n    redeclaration merges with an existing member from the baseType chain or from contracts[] —\n    contract completion uses the same rule as baseType refinement.\n\n    Local declaration properties (never inherited; only effects propagate):\n    • abstract=\&quot;true\&quot; — incomplete declaration; creates an implementation obligation\n    • final=\&quot;true\&quot; — seals the declaration; descendants cannot override\n    • override=\&quot;true\&quot; — confirms deliberate redefinition of an inherited member\n    Boolean properties require an explicit true or false — empty elements and bare attributes are\n    invalid. Preferred literals: lowercase true / false.\n\n    Modes:\n    • new ��� introduces a member; must not set override=\&quot;true\&quot; → else BML_OVERRIDE_WITHOUT_PARENT\n    • override — refines an inherited member; omit override when merging → BML_OVERRIDE_REQUIRED\n    Each redeclaration layer must set override=\&quot;true\&quot; again — override is not inherited.\n\n    Partial authoring: only the member name, override mode, and changed attributes need to be\n    specified — all other attributes are inherited from the parent definition. Omit unchanged type\n    (and other unchanged attributes such as bml:xml or defaults). On aggregations, restating an\n    identical type when only filling an inherited member → BML_REDUNDANT_AGGREGATION_TYPE (warning\n    V1). Declare type on an override only when refining or replacing the inherited type.\n\n    Abstract → implementation:\n    • Parent may omit required parts (e.g. property without type or value) when abstract=\&quot;true\&quot;\n    • Child implements with override=\&quot;true\&quot; and a locally complete declaration (abstract defaults\n      to false → locally concrete)\n    • To keep a member abstract in a child, redeclare with override=\&quot;true\&quot; abstract=\&quot;true\&quot;\n    • Abstract member left unimplemented on a concrete block → BML_ABSTRACT_MEMBER_NOT_IMPLEMENTED\n    Capability overrides supply a full implementation child element (not a boolean attribute).\n\n    Merge rules (resolveEffectiveMembers — baseType chain → contracts declaration order → local):\n    • Same member kind required (property overrides property, …)\n    • Only specified attrs replaced; unspecified attrs inherited\n    • Override matching key: (resolvedNamespace, normalizedLogicalName) — visibility prefixes\n      stripped; xmlns prefix aliases may differ if they resolve to the same namespace\n    • Visibility may widen (protected → public); narrowing → BML_VISIBILITY_NARROWING\n    • Member-level bml:xml may change on the same override\n    • Private members cannot be overridden → BML_FINAL_MEMBER_OVERRIDE\n    • final=\&quot;true\&quot; on parent prevents override → BML_FINAL_MEMBER_OVERRIDE\n\n    readOnly is orthogonal to final / abstract / override: it controls instance authoring only.\n    • Block definition — may declare and set readOnly members via value, composition, or partial\n      override\n    • Child Block definition — may override an inherited readOnly member (value/composition only;\n      cannot override a final member at all)\n    • Block instance — must not set a member whose effective definition has readOnly=true →\n      BML_READONLY_MEMBER_WRITE (after resolveEffectiveMembers on every BlockInstance)\n    • Expressions — may read readOnly members subject to visibility; renderers may read the BOM\n    A public readOnly member remains publicly readable. final blocks value overrides entirely;\n    readOnly does not.\n\n    Declared on org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition (abstract, final, override, readOnly,\n    visibility) and specialized on PropertyDefinition, AggregationDefinition, AssociationDefinition,\n    and CapabilityDefinition.\n  &lt;/documentation>\n\n  &lt;references>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:MemberDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;Defines\&quot;>\n      abstract, final, override, readOnly, visibility — local declaration properties.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:PropertyDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Property override completeness — type and value.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:AggregationDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Aggregation overrides — omit unchanged type; composition fill.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:CapabilityDefinition\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Capability overrides — implementation child element.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:MemberVisibility\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Visibility widening and private override prohibition.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:ModelingGuidelines\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Contracts merge order and abstract/final patterns.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:MemberAuthoring\&quot; relation=\&quot;ReadNext\&quot;>\n      Next — definition fields vs instance payloads (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; / &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;).\n    &lt;/see>\n  &lt;/references>\n\n&lt;/block>\n&quot;,&quot;numLines&quot;:103,&quot;startLine&quot;:1,&quot;totalLines&quot;:103}}}
