{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;stream_event&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;content_block_stop&quot;,&quot;index&quot;:1},&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;135897be-b601-465b-9bdf-06a65a427361&quot;}
{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;stream_event&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;message_delta&quot;,&quot;delta&quot;:{&quot;stop_reason&quot;:&quot;tool_use&quot;,&quot;stop_sequence&quot;:null,&quot;stop_details&quot;:null},&quot;usage&quot;:{&quot;input_tokens&quot;:2,&quot;cache_creation_input_tokens&quot;:2368,&quot;cache_read_input_tokens&quot;:34197,&quot;output_tokens&quot;:181,&quot;output_tokens_details&quot;:{&quot;thinking_tokens&quot;:72},&quot;iterations&quot;:[{&quot;input_tokens&quot;:2,&quot;output_tokens&quot;:181,&quot;cache_read_input_tokens&quot;:34197,&quot;cache_creation_input_tokens&quot;:2368,&quot;cache_creation&quot;:{&quot;ephemeral_5m_input_tokens&quot;:0,&quot;ephemeral_1h_input_tokens&quot;:2368},&quot;type&quot;:&quot;message&quot;}]},&quot;context_management&quot;:{&quot;applied_edits&quot;:[]}},&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;495d73f6-69e2-402b-8a87-eae99986488f&quot;}
{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;stream_event&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;message_stop&quot;},&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;616449ab-97e1-4fc3-8614-e737ac904b08&quot;}
{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;message&quot;:{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;tool_use_id&quot;:&quot;toolu_01GptYnSv4XTDKcMDL5EQLyW&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;tool_result&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;1\t&lt;!--\n2\t  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation\n3\t\n4\t  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.MemberAuthoring\n5\t-->\n6\t&lt;block\n7\t  xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n8\t  xmlns:xsi=\&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\&quot;\n9\t  xsi:schemaLocation=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd\n10\t                      \&quot;\n11\t  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n12\t  xmlns:def=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.definition\&quot;\n13\t  xmlns:diag=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.diagnostic\&quot;\n14\t  xmlns:doc=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.documentation\&quot;\n15\t  xmlns:task=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.task\&quot;\n16\t  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;>\n17\t\n18\t  &lt;name>MemberAuthoring&lt;/name>\n19\t  &lt;type>doc:MemberAuthoring&lt;/type>\n20\t  &lt;baseType>core:Documentation&lt;/baseType>\n21\t  &lt;is>A guide to definition versus instance member syntax&lt;/is>\n22\t  &lt;isNot>A general-purpose XML value or container wrapper&lt;/isNot>\n23\t\n24\t  &lt;summary>\n25\t    &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; and &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; belong only to member declarations. On a Block instance\n26\t    the Property element or attribute is already the value; the Aggregation element already holds\n27\t    the child Blocks. Do not wrap instance payloads in those definition fields.\n28\t  &lt;/summary>\n29\t\n30\t  &lt;keywords>value, composition, property, aggregation, instance, definition, member authoring&lt;/keywords>\n31\t\n32\t  &lt;documentation>\n33\t    LLMs repeatedly confuse member-declaration syntax with the syntax used when assigning members\n34\t    on Block instances. The two most common mistakes are wrapping an instance Property in\n35\t    &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; and wrapping instance Aggregation children in &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;.\n36\t\n37\t    Incorrect on a Block instance:\n38\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;Hello!&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n39\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n40\t\n41\t    Two contexts, never mixed:\n42\t\n43\t    1. Definition context — a Property or Aggregation is being declared inside &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;\n44\t       or &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt; (or an inherited member is filled on a Block definition).\n45\t    2. Instance context — a concrete Block instance receives Property values or Aggregation\n46\t       children.\n47\t\n48\t    &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; is the value field of def:PropertyDefinition. &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; is the\n49\t    composition field of def:AggregationDefinition. Both are definition-context fields. They are\n50\t    not general-purpose wrappers around instance payloads.\n51\t\n52\t    Critical authoring rule — inside a Block instance:\n53\t    • NEVER introduce &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; as a wrapper around a Property assignment\n54\t    • NEVER introduce &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; as a wrapper around Aggregation children\n55\t    Instead: the Property element (or Block attribute) contains the value; the Aggregation element\n56\t    contains the child Blocks. Group instance children with bml:container, not composition.\n57\t\n58\t    PROPERTIES — definition. Inside &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt; the child element is a PropertyDefinition.\n59\t    Its default value is the value field of that declaration. Element form is preferred when\n60\t    serializing definitions:\n61\t    &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;&amp;lt;description&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;BlockML core library&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/description&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/properties&amp;gt;\n62\t    Compact attribute form on the declaration is also valid:\n63\t    &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;&amp;lt;description value=\&quot;BlockML core library\&quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/properties&amp;gt;\n64\t    Do not specify both forms on the same declaration (conflicting payloads). Other declaration\n65\t    fields (type, readOnly, override, constraints, suggestions) stay on this PropertyDefinition\n66\t    element — they are not authored on domain instances.\n67\t\n68\t    PROPERTIES — Block instance. The instance is not a PropertyDefinition. It only supplies the\n69\t    payload. Attribute form is preferred:\n70\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock myProperty=\&quot;Hello!\&quot;/&amp;gt;\n71\t    Element form is the Property element with direct character content — the element itself is\n72\t    already the value container:\n73\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;Hello!&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n74\t    Incorrect — definition value field used as an instance wrapper:\n75\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;Hello!&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n76\t    Also incorrect as a wrapper (same category error):\n77\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty value=\&quot;Hello!\&quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n78\t    unless myProperty is actually named value (see exception below).\n79\t\n80\t    Exception — member whose name is value. PrimitiveEntity, TypeReferenceEntity, FilePathEntity\n81\t    and similar types declare a Property named value. Then value=\&quot;…\&quot; or &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;\n82\t    on the Block instance is ordinary instance syntax for that member, not a PropertyDefinition\n83\t    wrapper:\n84\t    &amp;lt;type:FilePathEntity value=\&quot;blockml-library.xsd\&quot;/&amp;gt;\n85\t    Annotation value facets (e.g. &amp;lt;scad:value&amp;gt; under a property declaration) are a separate\n86\t    namespace axis on PropertyDefinition.value — not instance wrappers. See doc:AnnotationModel.\n87\t\n88\t    AGGREGATIONS — definition. Inside &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt; the child element is an\n89\t    AggregationDefinition. Its initial/default child structure is the composition field:\n90\t    &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/aggregations&amp;gt;\n91\t    &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; is allowed only as that definition field, nested inside the aggregation\n92\t    member — never standalone (BML_STANDALONE_COMPOSITION).\n93\t\n94\t    AGGREGATIONS — Block instance. Child Block instances are placed directly inside the\n95\t    Aggregation element. There is no composition wrapper:\n96\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n97\t    Incorrect:\n98\t    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n99\t    The same rule applies recursively — a Block instance nested inside a definition composition\n100\t    still fills its own aggregations without a composition wrapper:\n101\t    &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myAggr&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;\n102\t      &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n103\t    &amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myAggr&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/aggregations&amp;gt;\n104\t    Outer &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; is valid (myAggr is an Aggregation definition). Inner\n105\t    &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; under content is invalid (content is populated on a Block instance).\n106\t\n107\t    On instances, the virtual grouping element is bml:container — not composition. Both\n108\t    composition (definitions) and bml:container (instances) host bml:if, bml:each, and bml:with.\n109\t\n110\t    Unified pattern:\n111\t    Definition Property → value attribute or &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; wrapper on the PropertyDefinition\n112\t    Definition Aggregation → &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; wrapper on the AggregationDefinition\n113\t    Instance Property → attribute on the Block, or direct Property element content\n114\t    Instance Aggregation → direct child Block instances (bml:container for grouping)\n115\t\n116\t    Capabilities on instances follow the Property pattern: attribute or child element, no extra\n117\t    wrapper. readOnly effective members must not be authored on instances\n118\t    (BML_READONLY_MEMBER_WRITE). Declared exception types are the throws aggregation on the Capability\n119\t    declaration — TypeReferenceEntity children (empty-QName sugar), not instance wrappers\n120\t    (doc:CapabilitySemantics).\n121\t  &lt;/documentation>\n122\t\n123\t  &lt;references>\n124\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:BlockAndInstance\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n125\t      Definition vs instance mental model.\n126\t    &lt;/see>\n127\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:PropertyDefinition\&quot; property=\&quot;value\&quot; relation=\&quot;Defines\&quot;>\n128\t      Definition-only value field on a Property declaration.\n129\t    &lt;/see>\n130\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:AggregationDefinition\&quot; property=\&quot;composition\&quot; relation=\&quot;Defines\&quot;>\n131\t      Definition-only composition field on an Aggregation declaration.\n132\t    &lt;/see>\n133\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:CapabilityDefinition\&quot; aggregation=\&quot;throws\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n134\t      throws aggregation — TypeReferenceEntity children, not instance wrappers.\n135\t    &lt;/see>\n136\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:CapabilitySemantics\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n137\t      Capability throws authoring — Java-style exception signatures.\n138\t    &lt;/see>\n139\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:CompositionModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;ReadNext\&quot;>\n140\t      Next — composition placement, recursion, bml:container, and instance IDs.\n141\t    &lt;/see>\n142\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:BmlDirectives\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n143\t      bml:container, bml:with, bml:each, bml:if on composition and instances.\n144\t    &lt;/see>\n145\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:AnnotationModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n146\t      Annotation value facets — not instance value wrappers.\n147\t    &lt;/see>\n148\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;core:PrimitiveEntity\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n149\t      Entity whose instance member is actually named value.\n150\t    &lt;/see>\n151\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;type:TypeReferenceEntity\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n152\t      Instance value=\&quot;…\&quot; because the member name is value — not a wrapper.\n153\t    &lt;/see>\n154\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;diag:BML_STANDALONE_COMPOSITION\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n155\t      composition outside an aggregation member on a definition.\n156\t    &lt;/see>\n157\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;task:FixCompositionPlacement\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n158\t      Procedure when composition is placed on an instance or left standalone.\n159\t    &lt;/see>\n160\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:PartialMemberOverrides\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n161\t      Filling inherited members on definitions; readOnly forbids instance writes.\n162\t    &lt;/see>\n163\t  &lt;/references>\n164\t\n165\t&lt;/block>\n166\t&quot;}]},&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;69535409-9aef-4bfd-a4ae-0d04f04df8e7&quot;,&quot;timestamp&quot;:&quot;2026-09-03T21:59:03.019Z&quot;,&quot;tool_use_result&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;file&quot;:{&quot;filePath&quot;:&quot;/Users/pksoftware/workspace-fh/blockml/node_modules/@blockml/core/blocks/org/blockml/bml/documentation/MemberAuthoring.bml&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;&lt;!--\n  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation\n\n  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.MemberAuthoring\n-->\n&lt;block\n  xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n  xmlns:xsi=\&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\&quot;\n  xsi:schemaLocation=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd\n                      \&quot;\n  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n  xmlns:def=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.definition\&quot;\n  xmlns:diag=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.diagnostic\&quot;\n  xmlns:doc=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.documentation\&quot;\n  xmlns:task=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.task\&quot;\n  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;>\n\n  &lt;name>MemberAuthoring&lt;/name>\n  &lt;type>doc:MemberAuthoring&lt;/type>\n  &lt;baseType>core:Documentation&lt;/baseType>\n  &lt;is>A guide to definition versus instance member syntax&lt;/is>\n  &lt;isNot>A general-purpose XML value or container wrapper&lt;/isNot>\n\n  &lt;summary>\n    &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; and &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; belong only to member declarations. On a Block instance\n    the Property element or attribute is already the value; the Aggregation element already holds\n    the child Blocks. Do not wrap instance payloads in those definition fields.\n  &lt;/summary>\n\n  &lt;keywords>value, composition, property, aggregation, instance, definition, member authoring&lt;/keywords>\n\n  &lt;documentation>\n    LLMs repeatedly confuse member-declaration syntax with the syntax used when assigning members\n    on Block instances. The two most common mistakes are wrapping an instance Property in\n    &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; and wrapping instance Aggregation children in &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;.\n\n    Incorrect on a Block instance:\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;Hello!&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n\n    Two contexts, never mixed:\n\n    1. Definition context — a Property or Aggregation is being declared inside &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;\n       or &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt; (or an inherited member is filled on a Block definition).\n    2. Instance context — a concrete Block instance receives Property values or Aggregation\n       children.\n\n    &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; is the value field of def:PropertyDefinition. &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; is the\n    composition field of def:AggregationDefinition. Both are definition-context fields. They are\n    not general-purpose wrappers around instance payloads.\n\n    Critical authoring rule — inside a Block instance:\n    • NEVER introduce &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; as a wrapper around a Property assignment\n    • NEVER introduce &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; as a wrapper around Aggregation children\n    Instead: the Property element (or Block attribute) contains the value; the Aggregation element\n    contains the child Blocks. Group instance children with bml:container, not composition.\n\n    PROPERTIES — definition. Inside &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt; the child element is a PropertyDefinition.\n    Its default value is the value field of that declaration. Element form is preferred when\n    serializing definitions:\n    &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;&amp;lt;description&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;BlockML core library&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/description&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/properties&amp;gt;\n    Compact attribute form on the declaration is also valid:\n    &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;&amp;lt;description value=\&quot;BlockML core library\&quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/properties&amp;gt;\n    Do not specify both forms on the same declaration (conflicting payloads). Other declaration\n    fields (type, readOnly, override, constraints, suggestions) stay on this PropertyDefinition\n    element — they are not authored on domain instances.\n\n    PROPERTIES — Block instance. The instance is not a PropertyDefinition. It only supplies the\n    payload. Attribute form is preferred:\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock myProperty=\&quot;Hello!\&quot;/&amp;gt;\n    Element form is the Property element with direct character content — the element itself is\n    already the value container:\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;Hello!&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n    Incorrect — definition value field used as an instance wrapper:\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;Hello!&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n    Also incorrect as a wrapper (same category error):\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myProperty value=\&quot;Hello!\&quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n    unless myProperty is actually named value (see exception below).\n\n    Exception — member whose name is value. PrimitiveEntity, TypeReferenceEntity, FilePathEntity\n    and similar types declare a Property named value. Then value=\&quot;…\&quot; or &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;\n    on the Block instance is ordinary instance syntax for that member, not a PropertyDefinition\n    wrapper:\n    &amp;lt;type:FilePathEntity value=\&quot;blockml-library.xsd\&quot;/&amp;gt;\n    Annotation value facets (e.g. &amp;lt;scad:value&amp;gt; under a property declaration) are a separate\n    namespace axis on PropertyDefinition.value — not instance wrappers. See doc:AnnotationModel.\n\n    AGGREGATIONS — definition. Inside &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt; the child element is an\n    AggregationDefinition. Its initial/default child structure is the composition field:\n    &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/aggregations&amp;gt;\n    &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; is allowed only as that definition field, nested inside the aggregation\n    member — never standalone (BML_STANDALONE_COMPOSITION).\n\n    AGGREGATIONS — Block instance. Child Block instances are placed directly inside the\n    Aggregation element. There is no composition wrapper:\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n    Incorrect:\n    &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n    The same rule applies recursively — a Block instance nested inside a definition composition\n    still fills its own aggregations without a composition wrapper:\n    &amp;lt;aggregations&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myAggr&amp;gt;&amp;lt;composition&amp;gt;\n      &amp;lt;myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;&amp;lt;content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;myns:Child/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/content&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myns:MyBlock&amp;gt;\n    &amp;lt;/composition&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/myAggr&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/aggregations&amp;gt;\n    Outer &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; is valid (myAggr is an Aggregation definition). Inner\n    &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; under content is invalid (content is populated on a Block instance).\n\n    On instances, the virtual grouping element is bml:container — not composition. Both\n    composition (definitions) and bml:container (instances) host bml:if, bml:each, and bml:with.\n\n    Unified pattern:\n    Definition Property → value attribute or &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; wrapper on the PropertyDefinition\n    Definition Aggregation → &amp;lt;composition&amp;gt; wrapper on the AggregationDefinition\n    Instance Property → attribute on the Block, or direct Property element content\n    Instance Aggregation → direct child Block instances (bml:container for grouping)\n\n    Capabilities on instances follow the Property pattern: attribute or child element, no extra\n    wrapper. readOnly effective members must not be authored on instances\n    (BML_READONLY_MEMBER_WRITE). Declared exception types are the throws aggregation on the Capability\n    declaration — TypeReferenceEntity children (empty-QName sugar), not instance wrappers\n    (doc:CapabilitySemantics).\n  &lt;/documentation>\n\n  &lt;references>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:BlockAndInstance\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Definition vs instance mental model.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:PropertyDefinition\&quot; property=\&quot;value\&quot; relation=\&quot;Defines\&quot;>\n      Definition-only value field on a Property declaration.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:AggregationDefinition\&quot; property=\&quot;composition\&quot; relation=\&quot;Defines\&quot;>\n      Definition-only composition field on an Aggregation declaration.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;def:CapabilityDefinition\&quot; aggregation=\&quot;throws\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      throws aggregation — TypeReferenceEntity children, not instance wrappers.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:CapabilitySemantics\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Capability throws authoring — Java-style exception signatures.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:CompositionModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;ReadNext\&quot;>\n      Next — composition placement, recursion, bml:container, and instance IDs.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:BmlDirectives\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      bml:container, bml:with, bml:each, bml:if on composition and instances.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:AnnotationModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Annotation value facets — not instance value wrappers.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;core:PrimitiveEntity\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Entity whose instance member is actually named value.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;type:TypeReferenceEntity\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Instance value=\&quot;…\&quot; because the member name is value — not a wrapper.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;diag:BML_STANDALONE_COMPOSITION\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      composition outside an aggregation member on a definition.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;task:FixCompositionPlacement\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Procedure when composition is placed on an instance or left standalone.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:PartialMemberOverrides\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Filling inherited members on definitions; readOnly forbids instance writes.\n    &lt;/see>\n  &lt;/references>\n\n&lt;/block>\n&quot;,&quot;numLines&quot;:166,&quot;startLine&quot;:1,&quot;totalLines&quot;:166}}}
