{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;stream_event&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;content_block_stop&quot;,&quot;index&quot;:1},&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;cfb21d8c-035b-497a-9903-8bdd6e73089b&quot;}
{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;message&quot;:{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;tool_use_id&quot;:&quot;toolu_01JPSpdYR5Fmni2WtWjxERAq&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;tool_result&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;1\t&lt;!--\n2\t  BlockML Definition — property member meta-model type\n3\t\n4\t  FQN: org.blockml.bml.definition.PropertyDefinition\n5\t  See docs/12_bom_object_model.md — PropertyDefinition · 02_mbml.md — Members.\n6\t-->\n7\t&lt;block\n8\t  xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n9\t  xmlns:xsi=\&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\&quot;\n10\t  xsi:schemaLocation=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd\n11\t                      \&quot;\n12\t  xmlns:bml=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation\&quot;\n13\t  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n14\t  xmlns:def=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.definition\&quot;\n15\t  xmlns:doc=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.documentation\&quot;\n16\t  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;>\n17\t\n18\t  &lt;name>PropertyDefinition&lt;/name>\n19\t  &lt;type>def:PropertyDefinition&lt;/type>\n20\t  &lt;baseType>def:MemberDefinition&lt;/baseType>\n21\t  &lt;is>A typed value member&lt;/is>\n22\t\n23\t  &lt;documentation>Describes a Block member that carries a scalar or structured value. Rendered as a\n24\t    child element inside the properties container; the XML element name is the property name\n25\t    (bml:xml=\&quot;${ #this.name }\&quot;). An optional XML prefix on the element name supplies the member\n26\t    namespace — for example ui5:width resolves via xmlns:ui5 to the canonical namespace stored in\n27\t    BOM namespace; unprefixed elements belong to the default namespace (empty string). The prefix\n28\t    itself is never stored. Member identity is (resolvedNamespace, localName). Maps to BOM\n29\t    PropertyDefinition (kind: \&quot;property\&quot;) with typeFqn, values[] (value-field entries with\n30\t    namespace), optional groups (inherited from MemberDefinition), and optional constraints (via\n31\t    ConstrainableDefinition) and suggestions. Convenience path value is the default-namespace entry.\n32\t    Property type must resolve to a ValueType branch. Scalar member fields (type, value) follow\n33\t    org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition placement rules on the PropertyDefinition\n34\t    declaration — element preferred on definitions. The value field is definition syntax only;\n35\t    it is not a wrapper around a Property assignment on a domain Block instance. On instances the\n36\t    Property is a Block attribute or the Property element's direct content\n37\t    (myProperty=\&quot;…\&quot; / &amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;) — see doc:MemberAuthoring. Structured\n38\t    children (groups, suggestions) remain elements. Every Property behaves as Optional — it has a\n39\t    value or has no value; there is no null. Declaration order among properties is significant for\n40\t    StructType positional mapping and Capability parameter order.\n41\t\n42\t    Value-field Annotation facets: nested under this property element, an Annotation-prefixed\n43\t    value element (e.g. scad:value from Annotation.Value) multiplies the value field along the\n44\t    Annotation namespace axis — same property identity, not a member QName and not scad:myProp.\n45\t    Parent context disambiguates from top-level &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;&amp;lt;scad:value/&amp;gt; members.\n46\t    See doc:AnnotationModel — Property value facets.&lt;/documentation>\n47\t\n48\t  &lt;references>\n49\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:MemberAuthoring\&quot; relation=\&quot;AuthoringGuide\&quot;>\n50\t      Definition value field vs instance Property payload — do not wrap instances in &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;.\n51\t    &lt;/see>\n52\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:AnnotationModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;AuthoringGuide\&quot;>\n53\t      Annotation value facets, parent-context rules, duplicate-namespace diagnostics.\n54\t    &lt;/see>\n55\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;core:ValueType\&quot; relation=\&quot;Requires\&quot;>\n56\t      Required branch for property payload types.\n57\t    &lt;/see>\n58\t    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:ConstraintsModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n59\t      Constraints and suggestions on properties.\n60\t    &lt;/see>\n61\t  &lt;/references>\n62\t\n63\t  &lt;properties>\n64\t    &lt;type type=\&quot;TypeReference(core:ValueType)\&quot; bml:xml=\&quot;element|attribute\&quot;>\n65\t      &lt;documentation>FQN of the property's ValueType (TypeExpression). Non-ValueType FQNs are invalid\n66\t        (BML_INVALID_PROPERTY_TYPE). Multiplicity, unions, generic applications, and instance\n67\t        configuration are expressed in the type string — e.g. Text{maxLength: 100}. On the\n68\t        PropertyDefinition declaration, element form is preferred (&amp;lt;type&amp;gt;Integer&amp;lt;/type&amp;gt;);\n69\t        attribute form is also valid (type=\&quot;Integer\&quot; on the property declaration element).&lt;/documentation>\n70\t    &lt;/type>\n71\t    &lt;value type=\&quot;Text\&quot; bml:xml=\&quot;element|attribute\&quot;>\n72\t      &lt;documentation>Default or computed value on the PropertyDefinition declaration inside\n73\t        &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt; — definition syntax only. May be a literal or a ${ … } expression.\n74\t        Element form is preferred (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;); compact attribute form on the\n75\t        declaration is also valid (value=\&quot;…\&quot;). Do not specify both on the same declaration.\n76\t        Absent value means Optional.empty — not null.\n77\t\n78\t        This field is not a wrapper used when assigning the Property on a domain Block instance.\n79\t        Instances use the member name as a Block attribute or as the Property element's direct\n80\t        content (width=\&quot;50\&quot; or &amp;lt;width&amp;gt;50&amp;lt;/width&amp;gt;) — never\n81\t        &amp;lt;width&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;50&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/width&amp;gt; and never &amp;lt;width value=\&quot;50\&quot;/&amp;gt;\n82\t        unless the member itself is named value (e.g. PrimitiveEntity.value,\n83\t        TypeReferenceEntity.value). See doc:MemberAuthoring.\n84\t\n85\t        Multiplicity: the value field may repeat along the Annotation namespace axis — canonical\n86\t        &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; (default namespace) plus optional Annotation Element facets such as\n87\t        &amp;lt;scad:value&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/scad:value&amp;gt; (Annotation.Value, name=\&quot;value\&quot;) nested under this\n88\t        property element. Stored in BOM values[] as PropertyValueEntry { namespace, value };\n89\t        convenience path value is the default-namespace entry. Facets do not change member\n90\t        identity (still this property's name) and are not the same as a top-level member\n91\t        &amp;lt;scad:value/&amp;gt; under &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;. Cross-namespace faceting is valid; same-namespace\n92\t        self-faceting is forbidden. Duplicate (namespace) → BML_DUPLICATE_PROPERTY_VALUE.\n93\t        See 02_mbml.md — Property value facets.&lt;/documentation>\n94\t    &lt;/value>\n95\t  &lt;/properties>\n96\t\n97\t  &lt;aggregations>\n98\t    &lt;suggestions type=\&quot;core:Block[]\&quot; bml:xml=\&quot;element\&quot;>\n99\t      &lt;documentation>Property-only metadata — suggested values for editors and renderers. Each child\n100\t        is a Block instance compatible with this property's typeFqn (Stage [8] —\n101\t        BML_SUGGESTION_TYPE_MISMATCH). Coarse aggregation bound is Block[] (BOM BlockInstance[]);\n102\t        exact compatibility is contextual: StructType / EnumType-adjacent instances use the\n103\t        ValueType itself (e.g. SizeXYZ); PrimitiveType properties use the matching *Entity wrapper\n104\t        (e.g. TextEntity for Text). Document order preserved in BOM suggestions[]. Must not appear\n105\t        on properties typed with an EnumType (BML_SUGGESTIONS_ON_ENUM). Suggestions are not\n106\t        enforced — authors may enter any compatible value. Always rendered as a suggestions child\n107\t        element; children use their declared type tag (same pattern as composition instances).\n108\t      &lt;/documentation>\n109\t    &lt;/suggestions>\n110\t  &lt;/aggregations>\n111\t&lt;/block>\n112\t&quot;}]},&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;2f49d976-9b8a-4ff7-87f0-23e0f02cf385&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;39bc0348-67ac-407b-a7d0-3e7dd40cd115&quot;,&quot;timestamp&quot;:&quot;2026-09-03T21:59:57.922Z&quot;,&quot;tool_use_result&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;file&quot;:{&quot;filePath&quot;:&quot;/Users/pksoftware/workspace-fh/blockml/node_modules/@blockml/core/blocks/org/blockml/bml/definition/PropertyDefinition.bml&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;&lt;!--\n  BlockML Definition — property member meta-model type\n\n  FQN: org.blockml.bml.definition.PropertyDefinition\n  See docs/12_bom_object_model.md — PropertyDefinition · 02_mbml.md — Members.\n-->\n&lt;block\n  xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n  xmlns:xsi=\&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\&quot;\n  xsi:schemaLocation=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd\n                      \&quot;\n  xmlns:bml=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation\&quot;\n  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n  xmlns:def=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.definition\&quot;\n  xmlns:doc=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.documentation\&quot;\n  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;>\n\n  &lt;name>PropertyDefinition&lt;/name>\n  &lt;type>def:PropertyDefinition&lt;/type>\n  &lt;baseType>def:MemberDefinition&lt;/baseType>\n  &lt;is>A typed value member&lt;/is>\n\n  &lt;documentation>Describes a Block member that carries a scalar or structured value. Rendered as a\n    child element inside the properties container; the XML element name is the property name\n    (bml:xml=\&quot;${ #this.name }\&quot;). An optional XML prefix on the element name supplies the member\n    namespace — for example ui5:width resolves via xmlns:ui5 to the canonical namespace stored in\n    BOM namespace; unprefixed elements belong to the default namespace (empty string). The prefix\n    itself is never stored. Member identity is (resolvedNamespace, localName). Maps to BOM\n    PropertyDefinition (kind: \&quot;property\&quot;) with typeFqn, values[] (value-field entries with\n    namespace), optional groups (inherited from MemberDefinition), and optional constraints (via\n    ConstrainableDefinition) and suggestions. Convenience path value is the default-namespace entry.\n    Property type must resolve to a ValueType branch. Scalar member fields (type, value) follow\n    org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition placement rules on the PropertyDefinition\n    declaration — element preferred on definitions. The value field is definition syntax only;\n    it is not a wrapper around a Property assignment on a domain Block instance. On instances the\n    Property is a Block attribute or the Property element's direct content\n    (myProperty=\&quot;…\&quot; / &amp;lt;myProperty&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/myProperty&amp;gt;) — see doc:MemberAuthoring. Structured\n    children (groups, suggestions) remain elements. Every Property behaves as Optional — it has a\n    value or has no value; there is no null. Declaration order among properties is significant for\n    StructType positional mapping and Capability parameter order.\n\n    Value-field Annotation facets: nested under this property element, an Annotation-prefixed\n    value element (e.g. scad:value from Annotation.Value) multiplies the value field along the\n    Annotation namespace axis — same property identity, not a member QName and not scad:myProp.\n    Parent context disambiguates from top-level &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;&amp;lt;scad:value/&amp;gt; members.\n    See doc:AnnotationModel — Property value facets.&lt;/documentation>\n\n  &lt;references>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:MemberAuthoring\&quot; relation=\&quot;AuthoringGuide\&quot;>\n      Definition value field vs instance Property payload — do not wrap instances in &amp;lt;value&amp;gt;.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:AnnotationModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;AuthoringGuide\&quot;>\n      Annotation value facets, parent-context rules, duplicate-namespace diagnostics.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;core:ValueType\&quot; relation=\&quot;Requires\&quot;>\n      Required branch for property payload types.\n    &lt;/see>\n    &lt;see type=\&quot;doc:ConstraintsModel\&quot; relation=\&quot;SeeAlso\&quot;>\n      Constraints and suggestions on properties.\n    &lt;/see>\n  &lt;/references>\n\n  &lt;properties>\n    &lt;type type=\&quot;TypeReference(core:ValueType)\&quot; bml:xml=\&quot;element|attribute\&quot;>\n      &lt;documentation>FQN of the property's ValueType (TypeExpression). Non-ValueType FQNs are invalid\n        (BML_INVALID_PROPERTY_TYPE). Multiplicity, unions, generic applications, and instance\n        configuration are expressed in the type string — e.g. Text{maxLength: 100}. On the\n        PropertyDefinition declaration, element form is preferred (&amp;lt;type&amp;gt;Integer&amp;lt;/type&amp;gt;);\n        attribute form is also valid (type=\&quot;Integer\&quot; on the property declaration element).&lt;/documentation>\n    &lt;/type>\n    &lt;value type=\&quot;Text\&quot; bml:xml=\&quot;element|attribute\&quot;>\n      &lt;documentation>Default or computed value on the PropertyDefinition declaration inside\n        &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt; — definition syntax only. May be a literal or a ${ … } expression.\n        Element form is preferred (&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;); compact attribute form on the\n        declaration is also valid (value=\&quot;…\&quot;). Do not specify both on the same declaration.\n        Absent value means Optional.empty — not null.\n\n        This field is not a wrapper used when assigning the Property on a domain Block instance.\n        Instances use the member name as a Block attribute or as the Property element's direct\n        content (width=\&quot;50\&quot; or &amp;lt;width&amp;gt;50&amp;lt;/width&amp;gt;) — never\n        &amp;lt;width&amp;gt;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt;50&amp;lt;/value&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/width&amp;gt; and never &amp;lt;width value=\&quot;50\&quot;/&amp;gt;\n        unless the member itself is named value (e.g. PrimitiveEntity.value,\n        TypeReferenceEntity.value). See doc:MemberAuthoring.\n\n        Multiplicity: the value field may repeat along the Annotation namespace axis — canonical\n        &amp;lt;value&amp;gt; (default namespace) plus optional Annotation Element facets such as\n        &amp;lt;scad:value&amp;gt;…&amp;lt;/scad:value&amp;gt; (Annotation.Value, name=\&quot;value\&quot;) nested under this\n        property element. Stored in BOM values[] as PropertyValueEntry { namespace, value };\n        convenience path value is the default-namespace entry. Facets do not change member\n        identity (still this property's name) and are not the same as a top-level member\n        &amp;lt;scad:value/&amp;gt; under &amp;lt;properties&amp;gt;. Cross-namespace faceting is valid; same-namespace\n        self-faceting is forbidden. Duplicate (namespace) → BML_DUPLICATE_PROPERTY_VALUE.\n        See 02_mbml.md — Property value facets.&lt;/documentation>\n    &lt;/value>\n  &lt;/properties>\n\n  &lt;aggregations>\n    &lt;suggestions type=\&quot;core:Block[]\&quot; bml:xml=\&quot;element\&quot;>\n      &lt;documentation>Property-only metadata — suggested values for editors and renderers. Each child\n        is a Block instance compatible with this property's typeFqn (Stage [8] —\n        BML_SUGGESTION_TYPE_MISMATCH). Coarse aggregation bound is Block[] (BOM BlockInstance[]);\n        exact compatibility is contextual: StructType / EnumType-adjacent instances use the\n        ValueType itself (e.g. SizeXYZ); PrimitiveType properties use the matching *Entity wrapper\n        (e.g. TextEntity for Text). Document order preserved in BOM suggestions[]. Must not appear\n        on properties typed with an EnumType (BML_SUGGESTIONS_ON_ENUM). Suggestions are not\n        enforced — authors may enter any compatible value. Always rendered as a suggestions child\n        element; children use their declared type tag (same pattern as composition instances).\n      &lt;/documentation>\n    &lt;/suggestions>\n  &lt;/aggregations>\n&lt;/block>\n&quot;,&quot;numLines&quot;:112,&quot;startLine&quot;:1,&quot;totalLines&quot;:112}}}
